`InputEventShortcut` instances are always constructed with `pressed = true` and never produce a corresponding “release” event, so with `ACTION_MODE_BUTTON_RELEASE` this handler will never set `action_mode_match` and the shortcut will stop working for `InputEventShortcut`-driven dispatch. Consider treating `InputEventShortcut` as an activation event (i.e., bypass action_mode matching for this event type, or treat it as a match for both modes).
```suggestion
	const bool is_shortcut_event = p_event->is_class("InputEventShortcut");
	bool action_mode_match = is_shortcut_event;
	if (!is_shortcut_event) {
		if (action_mode == ACTION_MODE_BUTTON_PRESS && p_event->is_pressed()) {
			action_mode_match = true;
		} else if (action_mode == ACTION_MODE_BUTTON_RELEASE && p_event->is_released()) {
			action_mode_match = true;
		}
