body:
The proposal seems correct though I would transform it like so: 
```C++
bool action_mode_match = false;
if (p_event->is_class("InputEventShortcut")) {
	action_mode_match = true;
} else if (action_mode == ACTION_MODE_BUTTON_PRESS && p_event->is_pressed()) {
	action_mode_match = true;
} else if (action_mode == ACTION_MODE_BUTTON_RELEASE && p_event->is_released()) {
	action_mode_match = true;
}
```

But it seems to me that, from what I can read on the documentation, it's not a really explicit behaviour. Maybe InputEventShortcut should ask for whether it is pressed or not? Could someone give me a feedback on how to handle this issue?
